From deef9d034fc29202c1ba5d7c06aa04d7f7019b8b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 19:18:46 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] kernel-settings: /tmp on disk, cleaned at every boot

Daniel: /tmp in RAM leaves no RAM. The first install of this version masks
tmp.mount, the way Debian's trixie release notes describe it (5.1.6), once:
an administrator's own tmp.mount is left alone, an unmask is kept on
upgrades, and a purge removes the mask it created. sparky-tmp.conf sorts
before systemd's tmp.conf, so its "D /tmp 1777 root root 10d" is the line
applied: /tmp is emptied at every boot (Debian's pre-trixie default) and
of files unused for 10 days (5.2.1). Container: 9 checks, including
systemd's Q line alone keeping the file across the boot run (the control).
VM: /tmp on ext4 after the reboot, a file from before the next boot gone.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus via Claude Code
